ht points, and most expert raters place the race in the Likely D column, though Cook and Inside Elections call it Lean D. Markets on Kalshi and Polymarket give Kotek roughly an 81% chance of winning. Yet the polling picture is murkier: a September DHM survey showed Drazan up two, and earlier Republican-sponsored polls had similar results. The race has been active, with the first debate in late September, Drazan broadening her message, and a large mystery outside donation drawing attention. The forecast expects Kotek to win by a modest margin, with meaningful uncertainty given the conflicting signals between markets and surveys.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.91, "margin": 7.23}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7143, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6673, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6685, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7753, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7762, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7967, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7478, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.743, "margin": 3.5}]}